{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"14 (21:707): Payment Success overlay renders correctly — dim layer over payment screen, white dialog, green circle + check, \"Payment done successfully.\", Continue button, nav Cart active. Only issue: top-left back icon = black square (shared with 13, as expected from clone).\n\n15 (21:731): Profile renders great — avatar, Aashifa, Personal Details (Email aashifa@gmail.com, Password dots), Business Address (N1 2LL, 216 St Paul's Rd, London, England, United Kingdom), Bank Account (204356XXXXXXX, Abhiraj Sisodiya, SBIN00428), Change Password outline + Save primary. Only issue: top-left back icon = black square.\n\nAll 15 frames now viewed. Remaining fixes:\n1. 08 (14:222): title clipped — wrap to 335 width.\n2. Black-square icons: back (4:60) on 11 (19:527), 12 (20:619), 13 (21:637), 14 (21:707), 15 (21:731); search (4:49) top-right on 11; heart (4:36) top-right on 12; Location/VIP/Return icons on 11 perks row. Small gray squares next to \"Size: 42\"/\"Qty: 1\"/Apply Coupon in 12 — those might be Chevron_Down 4:116 tinted, or they might be intentional color swatches. In the 12 screenshot, next to \"Size: 42\" and \"Qty: 1\" there were small gray rounded squares which look like they could be Chevron_Down dropdown indicators rendered as filled squares. The Apply Coupon row had a gray square too (probably a coupon icon or chevron). I'll replace those with fresh instances too if they map to icon masters.\n\nFix approach via use_figma:\n- For each frame, findAll INSTANCE nodes whose mainComponent is one of the icon masters (4:60 Back, 4:36 Wishlist, 4:49 Search, 4:150 Location, 4:155 VIP, 4:160 Return, 4:116 Chevron_Down, 4:111 Chevron_Right) and that are direct children of the frame (not inside nav instances). For each, record master id, x, y, width, height, then create a fresh instance and remove the old one.\n\nWait — but why did tint break them? tint() sets fills on all descendants. For stroke-based icons, setting fills makes the outline path filled → blob. Fresh instances will have component defaults. But do I want them tinted a specific color? The components' default color is presumably dark (#1A1D1E-ish or black). On 07 the back chevron rendered black and looked fine. On 09 the menu icon rendered dark fine. So fresh defaults are fine.\n\nBut careful about the perks icons on 11 — in the original kit design those are dark glyphs, fine.\n\nOne risk: findAll on a frame returns instances nested in sub-frames too but NOT inside other instances. The icons I placed are direct children of the frames (or children of header frames?). On 11 I built a custom header — icons might be direct children of frame 19:527. On 12, 13, 14, 15 likewise. The nav instances contain their own icons — those are inside instances and won't be returned by findAll, and they render fine anyway.\n\nAlso 12's \"small gray squares\" — need to identify what they are. Let me inspect first: run a read-only inspection call listing all INSTANCE nodes in 19:527, 20:619, 21:637, 21:707, 21:731 with name, mainComponent.id, x, y, w, h. Then decide which to replace.\n\nAlso inspect 08 title node (find text \"You want Authentic\" in 14:222, check its width/textAutoResize).\n\nLet me do the inspection in one call. Also list direct children of 12's product card area to find the gray squares — the squares next to \"Size: 42\"/\"Qty: 1\" might be instances of Chevron_Down 4:116. And Apply Coupon row square might be an icon too.\n\nInspection code:\n\n```js\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"5:2\");\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nconst out = [];\nfor (const fid of [\"14:222\",\"19:527\",\"20:619\",\"21:637\",\"21:707\",\"21:731\"]) {\n  const f = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(fid);\n  const insts = f.findAll(n => n.type === \"INSTANCE\");\n  for (const i of insts) {\n    out.push({f:fid, name:i.name, master:i.mainComponent ? i.mainComponent.id : \"?\", x:Math.round(i.absoluteTransform[0][2]), y:Math.round(i.absoluteTransform[1][2]), w:Math.round(i.width), h:Math.round(i.height), parent:i.parent.name});\n  }\n}\n// 08 title\nconst t08 = (await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"14:222\")).findOne(n => n.type===\"TEXT\" && n.characters.startsWith(\"You want\"));\nout.push({t08: t08 ? {w:t08.width, h:t08.height, x:t08.x, y:t08.y, ar:t08.textAutoResize} : null});\nreturn JSON.stringify(out);\n```\n\nHmm, findAll doesn't go inside instances, good. absoluteTransform gives absolute coords; that's fine for identification. Actually let me use relative x/y and parent name.\n\nNote: return values — use_figma returns console output or return? The plugin API eval — I've been returning values; earlier calls returned data successfully. Keep JSON small.\n\nThen the fix call replaces broken instances with fresh ones.\n\nLet me run inspection now.","signature":"ddf17856edba42a69a721385"}],"id":"b35b8d11-1b36-41b4-8600-a502c636f97c","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27c02197-3252-480f-900a-884ff728e974","uuid":"ade0cbe8-e124-4730-b168-6559f27c3e24","timestamp":"2026-10-30T21:15:24.864Z","thinking_duration_ms":21916}
